# Phase 2 brief: AI chat for InsightFlow

Phase 1 is complete (login, per-user dashboards, metrics catalog, query API,
widget builder). Read this brief and the existing REQUIREMENTS.md, then add a
"Phase 2 — AI chat" section to REQUIREMENTS.md. Do NOT write code yet. List
open questions and assumptions, then stop for my review.

## 1. Goal
Add an AI chat assistant to the dashboard. Users describe what they want in
plain language, the assistant builds the visualization, shows it in the chat,
and the user adds it to their dashboard with one click. The assistant can also
answer questions about the sales data using real numbers.

The assistant must use what Phase 1 already built:
- the same metrics catalog (measures and attributes),
- the same widget configuration format the builder produces,
- the same query API for all numbers,
- the same widget components to render visualizations.
It must NOT invent new chart types, measures, attributes, or numbers.

## 2. AI provider and key
- Provider: **xAI (Grok)**. Use the xAI API with a current Grok model that
  supports tool/function calling and structured outputs; check the xAI docs
  (docs.x.ai) for the latest model names and recommend one. The xAI API is
  OpenAI-compatible (base URL `https://api.x.ai/v1`), so an OpenAI-compatible
  SDK can be used. Keep the model name in `.env` (e.g. `AI_MODEL`) so it can
  be changed without code edits.
- The key is in `.env` as `XAPI_KEY`. Use it only on the server. It must never
  reach the browser, logs, or the repo. Add it to `.env.example` as a
  placeholder.
- The browser talks only to our own backend endpoint; the backend talks to
  the AI provider.

